      "hints": [
        "Use the binomial theorem $(1+y)^6 = 1 + \\binom{6}{1}y + \\binom{6}{2}y^2 + \\dots$ with $y = 3x$.",
        "Evaluate the terms: $1$, $6(3x) = 18x$, and $15(3x)^2 = 15(9x^2) = 135x^2$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Apply the binomial expansion formula to $(1 + 3x)^6$ in ascending powers of $x$:\n$$(1 + 3x)^6 = 1^6 + \\binom{6}{1} 1^5 (3x) + \\binom{6}{2} 1^4 (3x)^2 + \\dots$$",
        "Evaluate the binomial coefficients and compute the powers:\n$$1^6 = 1$$\n$$\\binom{6}{1}(3x) = 6(3x) = 18x$$\n$$\\binom{6}{2}(3x)^2 = 15(9x^2) = 135x^2$$",
        "State the first three terms of the expansion:\n$$1 + 18x + 135x^2$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Binomial Expansion": "Expands $(1+3x)^6$ up to $x^2$ correctly to get $1 + 18x + 135x^2$."
        },
